		tags = { "Mammals", "Artiodactyla" },
		aliases = { "Rooibok" },
		summary = "The **impala** or **rooibok** is a medium-sized [[Antelope|antelope]] found in [[East Africa|eastern]] and [[Southern Africa|southern Africa]]. The [[Monotypic taxon|only]] [[Neontology|extant]] member of the [[Genus|genus]] Aepyceros, and tribe Aepycerotini, it was first described to Europeans by German zoologist Hinrich Lichtenstein in 1812. Two [[Subspecies|subspecies]] are recognised—the grassland-dwelling **common impala** (sometimes referred to as the **Kenyan impala**), and the larger and darker **black-faced impala**, which lives in slightly more arid, scrubland environments. The impala reaches 70–92 cm at the shoulder and weighs 40–65 kg. It features a glossy, reddish brown coat. The male's slender, [[Lyre|lyre]]-shaped horns are 45–92 cm long.",
